Release DLL AdaptivePapyrusBudget 0.3.0 run through its real entry path (Plugin.cpp), 2026-11-11 12:27-12:40.
What this run was for: the new INI option [VMCatchUp] SkipWaitingCalls, read from the INI by the release DLL.

Build under test: 2026-11-11 12:26. DLL SHA-256 167A2C6933EBB7AC75E4ACA349769E642E4C29CAB76D57DE4E2B84E0EF3A5B35.
Not the DLL in dist/AdaptivePapyrusBudget-0.3.0-AE1170.zip, which is an older build.
Command per launch: build/catchup/run-release-check.ps1 -Sequence <name> -Mode <mode> [-Set "VMCatchUp|SkipWaitingCalls|true"]
Profile APB-CatchUp-Release, Save93, FramerateLimit 30, standing in Whiterun; the packaged INI with this run's values.
The game window was not checked for being in front, so the frame-time figures are not measurements.

RESULT
1. relchk-1226-acc, Mode=accelerate, option off: install line "skip waiting calls=false". Full-minute report: 1,799 frames,
   759 extra cycles, 1,659 extra calls, blocked_skips 658 (37% of frames), blocked_stops 670, front_skips 0, order_rebuilds 0,
   guard_violations 0, held_frames 154 (the hold after the load), gate_closes 0, 0.040 ms extra per frame, max 0.393 ms.
2. relchk-1226-skip, Mode=accelerate, SkipWaitingCalls=true: install line "skip waiting calls=true". Full-minute report:
   1,794 frames, 1,515 extra cycles (in 84% of the frames), 4,012 extra calls, front_skips 5,185, the queue rebuilt after 3
   cycles, blocked_skips 24, blocked_stops 2 (with the rule on these are cycles after which no reachable call could run),
   guard_violations 0, gate_closes 0, 0.087 ms extra per frame, max 0.561 ms. No "turned off" line.
3. relchk-1226-off, Mode=off with SkipWaitingCalls=true: the warning "[VMCatchUp] SkipWaitingCalls=true needs Mode=accelerate; it
   is ignored", then "VM catch-up is off"; nothing installed; the game ran its 90 s.
So the option reaches the rule through the release DLL, the new report fields are written, and the refusal outside accelerate
is logged. With the option on the extra cycles ran 2.0 times as often and dispatched 2.4 times as many queued calls as with
it off, in two separate launches of a standing scene (not a controlled comparison).

After each launch the two usual crash logs were written while the window was being closed (execute access violation at
0x7FF5DF460000 / 0x7FF5DF450000, also in the launch with nothing installed); no address of this project in their stack sections.

NOT COVERED: any menu during the run (no pausing menu was opened, so gate_closes stayed 0 and the closed-gate line never came),
saving, a quest or cell change, 42 FPS, a longer session. The first report line of each launch covers one frame only: the
report interval ended during the load.

The release test mod now holds this DLL and the packaged INI with everything off; the DLL and INI it held before are in
build/catchup/release-mod-before-relchk-1226.

